+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The repository does not contain a recorded full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95
+for the adversarial synthetic corpus with the 30-word frequent vocabulary from
+before the term-selection fix. Consequently, no pre-fix number is reported
+here.
+
+The fix was to discard a candidate query term when its document frequency is
+greater than one third of the store (for stores with at least 50 records),
+before sorting the remaining terms by inverse document frequency and selecting
+the top eight. This prevents low-signal vocabulary terms from forcing FTS5 to
+walk long posting lists.
+
+The repository also does not contain a recorded post-fix full-recall
+`UserPromptSubmit` p95 for that adversarial 30-word-vocabulary workload.
+
+These missing values should not be substituted with the other measurements in
+the repository. In particular, the documented 35.53 ms to 8.75 ms p95 change is
+a Python BM25 stage microbenchmark on a 50,000-record corpus, while 4.31 ms is
+the p95 of a separate end-to-end Rust hook measurement. Neither is identified
+as the adversarial synthetic full-recall benchmark requested here.
